From 380227d90a889ce11469706cb0f4ff4971835e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:55:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Miner films: a running miner plays its tier's film
 (owner-provided, 2026-10-27)

The owner's three Flow films (1920x1080, 10 s, with audio) are mapped by content to small / medium / large and re-encoded for the miner's square stage: 720x720 H.264, no audio, faststart, about 250-280 KB each. The machines are not always centred (the small miner's drill sits left), so nothing is cropped: the 16:9 frame is kept whole and the band above and below is the frame's own top / bottom row, stretched and blurred into the background gradient. Files are content-hashed and pinned in miningAssets.json 'videos' (src, bytes, sha256, source name/bytes/sha256); MinerMedia plays the film muted and looping only for a running miner, and keeps the image under reduced motion. CSP default-src 'self' covers same-origin media.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
